{
  "esm": "2.4.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "partial_wrt_param_instance",
    "description": "esm-spec §4.2 'Reading earlier documents': the body of `deriv` holds D(f, wrt: d) with `d` a parameter, left as written at the wire boundary. The instance binding d to \"x\" reads it as partial(f, wrt: x), which the rule `central_x` lowers; the instance binding d to \"t\" keeps the time derivative. The two instances rewrite to different bodies, so they become `deriv.variant1` / `deriv.variant2`.",
    "authors": [
      "one-operator-type conformance"
    ]
  },
